      "why": "pipelined_m had 0 feasible in its first 50 evals, but that search likely used m values that made latency too long for the 0.5 us p99 batch bound (ceil(N/m)+2 cycles at Fmax must fit the burst window). With m=2..4 and N=12..16, latency is 5-10 cycles; at a plausible Fmax of 100-200 MHz that is 25-100 ns, well under 500 ns. The key question is whether pipelined_m can beat pipelined on area by reducing register count (registers every m stages instead of every stage) while still meeting throughput (1 result/cycle) and the batch-latency bound. If it does, it could offer a lower-area point on the front. m is capped at 4 to keep latency short enough for the burst constraint."
