  "rationale": "The fleet facts show pipelined is the only family that has found feasible designs (26/50, best area 44176 um2), while pipelined_m, iterative, and unrolled_k have found none. The spec requires throughput >= 32 Msps (1 result/cycle at >= 32 MHz) and p99 batch latency <= 0.5 us for a 32-request burst, which strongly favors pipelined architectures. The previous pipelined search was too broad; this round narrows to the feasible region (W=14-18, N=12-16, tight guards) to drive area down and map the accuracy-area trade-off. pipelined_m gets a smaller share to test whether reduced register count can beat pipelined on area while still meeting the burst-latency bound, with m limited to 2-4 to keep latency short. The 60/40 split prioritizes refining the known-feasible family while still probing the potentially lower-area pipelined_m variant."
