  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established with 5 distinct designs covering area from 39,336 to 67,568 um^2 and accuracy from 12.5 to 16 bits. The minimum area design (pipelined, data_width=18, n_iter=14) meets all constraints: throughput 138 MSPS >= 32, max_abs_err 0.000175 <= 0.000244, and the system constraint sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 is satisfied (best seen 0.216 us). The pipelined_m family yielded 0 feasible designs, confirming pipelined is the dominant architecture for this spec. With 120/200 evaluations used and this being the final round, the front provides sufficient coverage for the selection rule (min area_um2) to pick the 39,336 um^2 design. No further exploration is needed."
